==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{compound|en|pineal|gland}}, from its pine-cone shape.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈpaɪ.niːəl ˌɡlænd/|/ˈpɪ.niːəl ˌɡlænd/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|anatomy}} A small, pinecone-shaped [[endocrine gland]] found near the centre of the brain that produces [[melatonin]].
#* {{quote-web
|date=2009-06-02
|author=Paul Fassa
|title=A Fluoride-Free Pineal Gland is More Important than Ever
|site=NaturalNews.com
|url=http://www.naturalnews.com/026364_fluoride_pineal_gland_sodium.html
|accessdate=2013-09-06
}}
#*: Good news though. Frequent exposure to outdoor sunshine, 20 minutes or so at a time, will help stimulate a fluoride calcified '''pineal gland'''. Just make sure you take off your hat. This is more important than most realize, because the pineal gland affects so much other enzyme and endocrine activity, including melatonin production.

